course: dictionary
lesson: 5591
title: Who is a librarian?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A librarian is a person who works in a library. Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «If a library book is damaged, you tell the librarian when you return it.» You tell the librarian about a damaged book, so the librarian must be the person in charge of the books.
explain: The clues in «A damaged library book is shown to the librarian, who can fix or replace it» tell you what a librarian does. They look after books, and they can fix them or replace them when they are damaged.
explain: Librarians also help people find books and information. «Ask the librarian» means you ask them for help. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "Ask the person who works in a library" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A librarian is a person who works in a library.
fact: A librarian looks after the books and helps people find books and information.
fact: «Librarian» is a noun. More than one librarian is librarians.
fact: In school, the school librarian helps you choose books and find reliable information online.
fact: If you lose or damage a library book, tell the librarian honestly. You may need to pay or replace it.
exercise: «If you lose a library book, tell the librarian; you may need to pay or replace it.» What should you do if you lose a library book? | Give it to a friend to keep | Hide it under your bed | *Tell the librarian | Throw it in the bin
exercise: In school, what can the school librarian help you do? | Mend the school roof | *Choose books and find reliable information online | Cook the lunches | Drive the school bus
exercise: What is a librarian? | A bird that likes reading | A shop that sells books | A large book with lots of pages | *A person who works in a library and helps people find books
test: «A damaged library book is shown to the librarian, who can fix or replace it.» What can the librarian do with a damaged book? | Sell it to a stranger | Read it aloud to the class | Throw it away without a word | *Fix it or replace it
test: Which word means one person who works in a library? | libraries | reading | library books | *librarian
exam: Tom says a librarian is a book you borrow. Which answer is correct? | Librarians are only found in schools | *Librarians are people who work in a library and help you find books | Librarians are books you borrow from the shelf | Librarians are shops that sell books
